  "tour": {
    "title": "Hesed: loyal love in its Old Testament range",
    "intro": "This tour starts with why hesed resists a one-word English equivalent, then follows it through four Old Testament settings: Ruth’s costly loyalty, David’s covenant generosity, and Micah’s call to make this kind of love visible in public life. Listen for the common thread—and for what each setting adds.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:loyal-love-god",
        "startSec": 55,
        "endSec": 341,
        "why": "Begin here for the basic definition and the translation question. The speakers describe hesed as combining “being generous with being loyal” and “deep affection,” expressed through concrete acts that fulfill a promise. They also explain why English Bibles variously say “mercy,” “loving kindness,” “love,” or “steadfast love,” and note that about three-quarters of its occurrences concern God while the rest show humans practicing it.",
        "episodeTitle": "The Loyal Love of God",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/e530ba3f-428a-4ef5-828c-34800da4963f/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=e530ba3f-428a-4ef5-828c-34800da4963f",
        "durationSec": 4105,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "spoken-gospel:podcast:a88b1fb7-fd1c-415f-b24c-98322c767992",
        "startSec": 917,
        "endSec": 1075,
        "why": "Now hear hesed in Ruth 1 as personal, costly, covenant-shaped loyalty. The teacher explains Naomi’s “deal kindly” as hesed and compares “covenant faithfulness,” “longstanding loyalty,” and “steadfast love,” preferring loyalty because it gives concrete shape to the word. Ruth’s pledge—“Your people shall be my people, your God my God”—shows that hesed is more than a warm feeling: it is choosing faithful belonging when Naomi has nothing to offer.",
        "episodeTitle": "Ruth 1-2: God Fills What's Empty",
        "sourceId": "spoken-gospel",
        "source": "Spoken Gospel",
        "audioUrl": "https://traffic.megaphone.fm/SPG9761838334.mp3?updated=1664486106",
        "durationSec": 3645,
        "adInsertionDrift": true
      },
      {
        "recordId": "forty-minutes-ot:podcast:478e6896-2d24-4806-ac5f-4db234766229",
        "startSec": 1425,
        "endSec": 1656,
        "why": "This clip widens the range from family loyalty to royal action toward a potential enemy. In 2 Samuel 9, David asks whether anyone remains from Saul’s house—not to eliminate a rival, but to show hesed “for the sake of Jonathan.” The teachers stress that David wants to show “the kindness of God,” so hesed here becomes covenant loyalty, generosity, and divine-like welcome extended to Mephibosheth.",
        "episodeTitle": "2 Samuel 8:9-9:13 (Episode 267)",
        "sourceId": "forty-minutes-ot",
        "source": "40 Minutes in the Old Testament",
        "audioUrl": "https://adbarker.com/stream/tfVE3XBxC9JCmb97VsZt7vpT/traffic.libsyn.com/secure/40minot/40_Min_ep_667.mp3?dest-id=245197",
        "durationSec": 2471,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:loyal-love-god",
        "startSec": 1550,
        "endSec": 1765,
        "why": "Finish with Micah 6:8, where hesed becomes a public and ethical vocation rather than merely a private relationship. The speakers distinguish “do justice,” “love hesed,” and “walk humbly,” then insist that hesed is “not a feeling” but “a visible action that shows your posture in the relationship.” Their emphasis on long-term commitment and stepping beyond immediate gratification shows why “loyal love” captures more than either kindness or emotion alone.",
        "episodeTitle": "The Loyal Love of God",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/e530ba3f-428a-4ef5-828c-34800da4963f/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=e530ba3f-428a-4ef5-828c-34800da4963f",
        "durationSec": 4105,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      }
    ],
    "closing": "Taken together, these clips suggest that hesed is not untranslatable so much as uncontainable in one English word. “Loyal love,” “steadfast love,” “covenant faithfulness,” and “loving kindness” each illuminate part of it; the stories show the whole by putting affection, commitment, generosity, and concrete action together.",
    "totalSeconds": 890
  },
